        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for the Linux Kernel (Live Patch 59 for SUSE Linux Enterprise 15 SP4)",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "\nThis update for the SUSE Linux Enterprise Kernel 5.14.21-150400.24.240 fixes various security issues:\n\nThe following security issues were fixed:\n\n- CVE-2026-74469: sctp: prevent peer transport count overflow (bsc#1280693).\n- CVE-2026-89551: SUNRPC: xdr_buf_trim: clamp buf-\u003elen to avoid underflow (bsc#1280728).\n- CVE-2026-89674: nfsd: fix XDR length calculation in nfsd4_ff_encode_layoutget (bsc#1280285).\n- CVE-2026-98432: ipv4: free inet_opt and ireq_opt after an RCU grace period (bsc#1285686).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
